{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d65f544-c55c-4e7c-a4c5-65608fcbb450","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A converging lens brings parallel rays toward its far focal point. Place an upright object beyond the near focal point.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Converging lens: ray diagram"},{"op":"figure","id":"diagram","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-5.5,5.5],"y":[-2.8,2.8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"axis","from":[-5,0],"to":[5,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","id":"lens","from":[0,-2.5],"to":[0,2.5]},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[-0.22,2.2],[0,2.5],[0.22,2.2]]},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[-0.22,-2.2],[0,-2.5],[0.22,-2.2]]},{"kind":"point","id":"near_focus","at":[-2,0],"label":"F"},{"kind":"point","id":"far_focus","at":[2,0],"label":"F′"},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"segment","id":"object","from":[-4,0],"to":[-4,2],"arrow":true,"label":"object"},{"kind":"point","id":"tip","at":[-4,2]}]},{"op":"equation","id":"setup","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"d_o=2f"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d65f544-c55c-4e7c-a4c5-65608fcbb450","step":{"id":"s2","script":"From the object's tip, draw a ray parallel to the axis. After the lens, it passes through the far focal point.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"parallel_ray","on":"diagram","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"entry","at":[0,2]},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"tip"},"to":{"at":"entry"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","id":"refracted","from":{"at":"entry"},"to":[4.6,-2.6],"arrow":true}]},{"op":"text","id":"rule_one","anchor":{"el":"setup","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Parallel ray → far focus"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d65f544-c55c-4e7c-a4c5-65608fcbb450","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A second ray passes straight through the lens's center. Where the two outgoing rays meet, the image tip forms.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"central_ray","on":"diagram","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"tip"},"to":{"at":"center"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","id":"straight","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[4.8,-2.4],"arrow":true},{"kind":"point","id":"image_tip","at":{"hit":["refracted","straight"]}}]},{"op":"text","id":"rule_two","anchor":{"el":"rule_one","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Center ray → straight through"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Is the image upright or inverted, and is it real or virtual?","expected_gist":"Inverted and real: the outgoing rays actually meet below the axis."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d65f544-c55c-4e7c-a4c5-65608fcbb450","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Draw the image down from the axis to the intersection. At twice the focal length, the image is real, inverted, and equal in size.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"image_result","on":"diagram","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[4,0],"to":{"at":"image_tip"},"arrow":true,"label":"image"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-2.7],"to":[4,-2.7],"label":"2f"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"rule_two","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"d_i=2f,\\qquad m=-\\frac{d_i}{d_o}=-1"},{"op":"text","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"result","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Real • inverted • same size"}],"checkpoint":null}}
